WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.859
The context window: the agent’s working memory.

2
00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:07.192
Everything the model knows during a session sits in its context window.

3
00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:14.981
The Claude Code docs list what goes in: the conversation history, file contents it has read, command outputs, your CLAUDE.

4
00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:24.797
md files, auto memory, loaded skills, system instructions, and the names of available MCP tools (their full schemas load on demand).

5
00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:31.179
Claude Code also adds its own context, such as a note when a file it read earlier changed on disk.

6
00:00:31.459 --> 00:00:34.381
Running /context shows what is using space.

7
00:00:34.661 --> 00:00:37.520
Three facts follow, and each changes how you work.

8
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.869
Tool output is the big consumer.

9
00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:45.099
A full test log, a wide search, or a large file can cost far more than your prompts.

10
00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:57.347
Anthropic’s context-engineering post calls the problem context rot: as context grows, the model’s ability to use any one piece of it degrades, so more is not free even when it fits.

11
00:00:57.627 --> 00:00:59.333
Long sessions get compacted.

12
00:00:59.613 --> 00:01:03.325
As the window fills, Claude Code summarizes the conversation.

13
00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:11.627
The summary keeps your requests and key code, but the docs warn that detailed instructions from early in the conversation may be lost.

14
00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:15.277
The memory docs add the counterpart: the project-root CLAUDE.

15
00:01:15.557 --> 00:01:19.419
md is re-read from disk and re-injected after compaction.

16
00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:24.307
So a rule you typed in chat at minute five is fragile, and the same rule in CLAUDE.

17
00:01:24.587 --> 00:01:25.888
md is durable.

18
00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:32.739
You can steer compaction with /compact plus a focus, or a “Compact Instructions” section in CLAUDE.

19
00:01:33.019 --> 00:01:33.829
md.

20
00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:35.624
Sessions are independent.

21
00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:38.144
A new session starts with a fresh context.

22
00:01:38.424 --> 00:01:40.664
Continuity comes from files (CLAUDE.

23
00:01:40.944 --> 00:01:46.491
md, auto memory, your git history, a spec), not from the model remembering yesterday.

24
00:01:46.771 --> 00:01:56.627
That is a feature: /clear between unrelated tasks is free, gives better answers, and costs less, because every request resends the whole conversation.
